Bound the ModVfsTable trace dedup set, not just the file (GOW_MOD_VFS_TRACE only; no gameplay change)

`GOW_MOD_VFS_TRACE` documents a bounded trace ("Bounded; misses are included"), and the file itself stops at
`kMaxTraceEntries`. The dedup set did not: `appendTrace` inserted every new guest path into `m_traceSeen` before
checking the cap, so a session that looked up many distinct paths (or a trace left on by mistake) kept growing the
set for the whole run even after the file stopped at 4096 lines. The cap is now checked first, so neither the file
nor the set grows past `kMaxTraceEntries`. The miss-first classification comment is kept, moved above the dedup probe.

Only the diagnostics path changes: with `GOW_MOD_VFS_TRACE` unset nothing calls `appendTrace`, so the default
gameplay path is untouched. `ps2EntryRunner` rebuilt clean after the edit. Six 63 s ship-deck runs (three per
binary, alternating before/after the change, 0.5x, loaded window t=50-60 s) reach `state=11 levelReady=1` with
`anomalies=0`; `vu_ms` 4680.4 vs the patch-89 window 4651.3 (+0.6 %, inside the +/-1 % band).

diff --git a/PS2Recomp/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/mod_vfs_table.cpp b/PS2Recomp/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/mod_vfs_table.cpp
index 8df84a0..ca62915 100644
--- a/PS2Recomp/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/mod_vfs_table.cpp
+++ b/PS2Recomp/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/mod_vfs_table.cpp
@@ -171,17 +171,16 @@ void ModVfsTable::writeStats() const
 void ModVfsTable::appendTrace(const std::string &key, bool hit) const
 {
     std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(m_traceMutex);
-    if (m_traceSeen.emplace(key).second)
-    {
-        if (m_traceCount++ >= kMaxTraceEntries)
-            return;
-        m_traceOut << (hit ? 'H' : 'M') << '\t' << key << '\n';
-        m_traceOut.flush();
-    }
-    else
-    {
-        // A path that was first looked up as a miss and is later overridden keeps its first line: the table does not
-        // change while the game runs, so the first classification is also the final one.
-    }
+    // Bound the dedup set as well as the file: once the cap is reached a new path must not be remembered, otherwise
+    // a trace left on by mistake grows with every distinct guest path for the whole session.
+    if (m_traceCount >= kMaxTraceEntries)
+        return;
+    // A path that was first looked up as a miss and is later overridden keeps its first line: the table does not
+    // change while the game runs, so the first classification is also the final one.
+    if (!m_traceSeen.emplace(key).second)
+        return;
+    ++m_traceCount;
+    m_traceOut << (hit ? 'H' : 'M') << '\t' << key << '\n';
+    m_traceOut.flush();
 }
 }
